      "content": "The US government's current policies, including expanded use of technology, increased border patrol presence, and asylum processing wait times, have had some success in deterring and managing migrant traffic. However, the sheer volume of crossings and asylum claims has overwhelmed agency resources, raising questions about the effectiveness and cost of current measures. Increasing funding and personnel might alleviate pressure, but fundamental shifts in immigration policy and progress toward long-term border security solutions remain elusive.",
